Hi Maria,

Thanks for the productive call yesterday. Below are the action items
we agreed on -- I've assigned owners and target dates.

SUPPLY CHAIN SYNC -- ACTION ITEMS (Aug 20 Call)
================================================

1. CONTAINER ALLOCATION (Owner: David N. | Due: Aug 28)
   - Confirm 40-ft reefer container availability for the Sep 15
     Shanghai-to-Rotterdam shipment.
   - Share updated rate card with PartnerCo procurement.

2. CUSTOMS PRE-CLEARANCE (Owner: Maria T. | Due: Aug 26)
   - Submit HS tariff codes for the new SKU batch (PCB-4400 series)
     to the Rotterdam customs broker.
   - Confirm whether preferential duty treatment applies under
     the EU-Singapore FTA.

3. WAREHOUSE CAPACITY (Owner: Logistics Ops | Due: Sep 1)
   - Validate that Rotterdam Warehouse B has sufficient pallet
     positions for the projected +20% volume increase in Q4.
   - Provide overflow options if capacity is constrained.

4. TRACKING INTEGRATION (Owner: David N. + PartnerCo IT | Due: Sep 5)
   - Complete API integration testing for real-time container
     tracking (Maersk TradeLens -> PartnerCo ERP).
   - Share Postman collection with PartnerCo dev team.

Next sync call is scheduled for Thursday, Aug 27 at 09:00 SGT /
03:00 CEST. Calendar invite to follow.

Please flag any blockers early so we can keep the Sep 15 sailing
date on track.

Best,
David Nakamura
Director of Operations | Global Logistics International
Mobile: +65 9123 4567
d.nakamura@globallogistics.io

